  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Tailored Post Arrival Assistance and Sustainable Reintegration to Returnees in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims at providing tailored reception and post arrival assistance migrants in a vulnerable situation upon their return to Venezuela, as well as individual or community-based reintegration support. Mental health and psychosocial support will be also provided to returnees as well as to their families and members of the community, through the deployment of a network of psychologist and social workers. IOM AVR scheme is composed by three stages: pre-departure, travel assistance and reception and post arrival assistance. IOM carefully monitors all stages to gather beneficiaries&#xb4; perspectives, safeguard that all persons that received AVR assistance from IOM have done so based on a well-informed decision and on the basis of freedom of choice and to tailor programming according to the needs of beneficiaries, which may differ according to their specific situation; however, all programming is needs-based, and targeted according to varying social, psychosocial, and economic necessities. This project will focus on the third stage of the scheme, as pre departure assistance and travel assistance will be provided by other IOM missions in Latin America and Caribbean countries.</narrative>
  </description>
